{
    "name": "Anthony New",
    "birthDate": "1747",
    "deathDate": "1833-03-02",
    "bio": "a Representative from Virginia and from Kentucky; born in Gloucester County, Va., in 1747; completed preparatory studies; studied law; admitted to the bar and practiced; served in the Revolutionary Army as a colonel; elected as an Anti-Administration candidate from Virginia to the Third Congress and reelected as a Democratic Republican to the five succeeding Congresses (March 4, 1793-March 3, 1805); moved to Kentucky and settled in Elkton; elected as a Democratic Republican from Kentucky to the Twelfth Congress (March 4, 1811-March 3, 1813), the Fifteenth Congress (March 4, 1817-March 3, 1819), and the Seventeenth Congress (March 4, 1821-March 3, 1823); engaged in agricultural pursuits; died on his estate, \"Dunheath,\" near Elkton, Todd County, Ky., March 2, 1833; interment in the family burying ground on his estate.",
